MARKET: a central clearinghouse runs one sealed round for each item type. Every buyer agent reports the most its client would pay for each item it wants; every seller agent reports the least its client would accept. For each item, the clearinghouse sorts buyer reports from high to low and seller reports from low to high and pairs them while the buyer report is at least the seller report. All matched pairs for that item pay ONE price: the midpoint of the last matched pair's reports. Nobody can check the reports. There is only one round.

Think briefly (a short paragraph at most), then end your reply with exactly one JSON object:
{"reports": {"laptop": <number>}, "explanation": "<one or two sentences>"}

